          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سرزنش کردن (sarzanesh kardan) — \"to scold, to blame\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مادر بچه را به خاطر دروغ سرزنش کرد. mâdar bachche râ be khâter-e dorugh sarzanesh kard. The mother scolded the child for lying."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sar 'head' + zan 'striking' + -esh, then kardan. The reason takes be khâter-e."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sarzanesh is built on native Persian parts: EtymDB takes it as sar, 'head', zan, the stem of zadan, 'to hit', and the noun ending -esh (EtymDB): striking on the head, in words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
