          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دلداری دادن (deldâri dâdan) — \"to comfort, to console\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دوستم بعد از امتحان به من دلداری داد. dustam ba'd az emtehân be man deldâri dâd. My friend comforted me after the exam."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "del 'heart' + dâr 'keeping' + -i, then dâdan 'to give'. The person comforted takes be."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "deldâri is built on native Persian parts: del, 'heart', which EtymDB traces to Middle Persian (EtymDB), dâr, the stem of dâshtan, and -i: keeping someone's heart up. dâdan, 'to give', is inherited."
            }
          ]
        },
